</div>

:: R6-EverywhereAtOnce [release6]
Over the next few days, EthX-chan continues to echo through the internet without me doing anything. I'm not streaming as her. I'm not posting about her. But she's alive in the machine.

A compilation channel edits my best moments from the stream into a three minute video titled "EthX-chan Best Moments, Femboy Gamer Goes Viral." It gets a hundred eighty thousand views in four days. The comments are a spectrum from supportive to horny to philosophical.

"this is what happens when men stop being afraid of being pretty." "I would literally die for EthX-chan." "bruh I'm not even into femboys but something about this person is different." "the way he read that good girl donation, he liked it, like LIKED it liked it. I know that face."

I read that last comment seven times. Close the tab. Open the tab. Read it again.

Someone has lip synced over my stream audio, dubbing my reactions into a thirst trap format. It has four hundred thousand views. My face. My voice. My reactions. Remixed and repackaged into content I didn't create and can't control.

The algorithm has opinions about me now. It decided who I am based on one night in a plaid skirt, and it's not interested in hearing counterarguments.

